0.71 -119.2 -79.83 -120.08 -78.74 -120.08 C -77.65 -120.08 -76.77 -119.2 -76.77 -118.11 Z M -78.74 -118.11"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -82.2 -131.92)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.F1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -70.87 L 0 -97.79"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.32pt" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -97.79)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -1.66 2.21 C -1.52 1.38 0 0.14 0.42 0 C 0 -0.14 -1.52 -1.38 -1.66 -2.21"></path></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>We construct families of covers parametrized by <math id="S2.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in B</annotation></semantics></math> by
attaching a variable family of covers <math id="S2.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>
to a fixed cover <math id="S2.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta{\colon}E\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta{\colon}E\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the pullbacks of the divisor classes <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> along the map from <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{d_{1},g_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{d_{1},g_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> given by <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> likewise. Let <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> be the intersection number of <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Br(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Br</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Br(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> with a horizontal section of <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}\times B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}\times B</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[p]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[p]</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[q]</annotation></semantics></math>) the class of <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(B)</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(B)</annotation></semantics></math>) on <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmclaim1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmclaim1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span><span id="Thmclaim1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmclaim1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmclaim1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmclaim1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With the notation above, we have</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\deg T_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\deg T_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\deg T_{\alpha}+3([p]+[q])\cdot\Ram(\alpha)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Ram</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\deg T_{\alpha}+3([p]+[q])\cdot\Ram(\alpha),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\deg D_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\deg D_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\deg D_{\alpha}+(2g_{2}+2d_{2}-2)e+4e-4([p]+[q])\cdot\Ram(\alpha),\text{ and }" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Ram</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> and</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\deg D_{\alpha}+(2g_{2}+2d_{2}-2)e+4e-4([p]+[q])\cdot\Ram(\alpha),\text{ and }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\deg\Delta_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\deg\Delta_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\deg\Delta_{\alpha}+[p]^{2}+[q]^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\deg\Delta_{\alpha}+[p]^{2}+[q]^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of the claim.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The pullback of the line bundle <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{d,g}^{ns}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{d,g}^{ns}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{p/X}\otimes N_{p^{\prime}/E})\otimes(N_{q/E}\otimes N_{q^{\prime}/E})\otimes O_{B}(\Delta_{\alpha})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{p/X}\otimes N_{p^{\prime}/E})\otimes(N_{q/E}\otimes N_{q^{\prime}/E})\otimes O_{B}(\Delta_{\alpha}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p/X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p/X}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the normal bundle of <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, and so on. The third equation follows.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a generic <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in B</annotation></semantics></math>, the point of <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{d,g}^{ns}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{d,g}^{ns}</annotation></semantics></math> given by <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{b}{\colon}C_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{b}{\colon}C_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> does not lie in <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. We have the following specializations:</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has a fiber of the form <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3p_{1}+p_{2}+\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3p_{1}+p_{2}+\dots</annotation></semantics></math>. Such <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>’s are precisely the points of <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, each contributing <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg T_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg T_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> has a fiber of the form <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2p_{1}+2p_{2}+p_{3}+\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2p_{1}+2p_{2}+p_{3}+\dots</annotation></semantics></math>. Such <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>’s are precisely the points of <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, each contributing <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg D_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg D_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A branch point of <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with a branch point of <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta{\colon}E\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta{\colon}E\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. There are <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2g_{2}+2d_{2}-2)e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2g_{2}+2d_{2}-2)e</annotation></semantics></math> such <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>’s, each contributing <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg D_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg D_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>) is a ramification point of <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>. We compute the intersection multiplicity of <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> at such a point by looking at a versal deformation space of <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>. We may restrict <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> over an analytic neighborhood <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math>). Let <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> be a coordinate on <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{b}^{-1}(U)\to U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{b}^{-1}(U)\to U</annotation></semantics></math> has the form</p>
<table id="S2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U[y]/(y^{3}-xy)\sqcup U\sqcup\dots\sqcup U\to U." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U[y]/(y^{3}-xy)\sqcup U\sqcup\dots\sqcup U\to U.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I2.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A versal deformation of this cover is given over <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U[y]/(y^{3}-xy-sx-t)\sqcup U\sqcup\dots\sqcup U\to U." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U[y]/(y^{3}-xy-sx-t)\sqcup U\sqcup\dots\sqcup U\to U.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I2.i4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In
<math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]</annotation></semantics></math>, the divisor <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> does not contain the origin,
and hence the intersection number of <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. The divisor <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\subset\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\subset\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The curve <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> approaches the origin along the locus where
<math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U[y]/(y^{3}-xy-sx-t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U[y]/(y^{3}-xy-sx-t)</annotation></semantics></math> is singular, namely along <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{3}+t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{3}+t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We
deduce that the intersection number of <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>. There are <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[p]\cdot\Ram(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Ram</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[p]\cdot\Ram(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[q]\cdot\Ram(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Ram</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[q]\cdot\Ram(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>) such <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>’s, each contributing 3 to <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg T_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg T_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>) is not a ramification point of
<math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, but lies over a branch point. Again, we look at a
versal deformation of <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case,
<math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{b}^{-1}(U)\to U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{b}^{-1}(U)\to U</annotation></semantics></math> has the form</p>
<table id="S2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U[y]/(y^{2}-x)\sqcup U[z]/(z^{2}-x^{2})\sqcup U\sqcup\dots\sqcup U\to U." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U[y]/(y^{2}-x)\sqcup U[z]/(z^{2}-x^{2})\sqcup U\sqcup\dots\sqcup U\to U.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I2.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A versal deformation of this cover is given over <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U[y]/(y^{2}-x)\sqcup U[z]/(z^{2}-x^{2}-sx-t)\sqcup U\sqcup\dots\sqcup U\to U." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊔</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U[y]/(y^{2}-x)\sqcup U[z]/(z^{2}-x^{2}-sx-t)\sqcup U\sqcup\dots\sqcup U\to U.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I2.i5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]</annotation></semantics></math>, the divisor <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> does not
contain the origin, and hence the intersection number of <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. The divisor <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subset\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>Spec</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subset\operatorname{Spec}{\bf C}[s,t]</annotation></semantics></math> is
defined by <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The curve <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> approaches the origin along
the locus where <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U[z]/(z^{2}-x^{2}-sx-t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U[z]/(z^{2}-x^{2}-sx-t)</annotation></semantics></math> is singular, namely along
<math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{2}-4t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}-4t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We deduce that the intersection number of <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us count the number of such points, first
for <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, and analogously for <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>. The points <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> for which
<math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> is not a ramification point but lies over a branch point
correspond to the intersection points of <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Br(\alpha)\cap\{0\}\times B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Br</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Br(\alpha)\cap\{0\}\times B</annotation></semantics></math> which are not the images of the points of
<math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ram(\alpha)\cap p(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Ram</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ram(\alpha)\cap p(B)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note, however, that the image of a
point of <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ram(\alpha)\cap p(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Ram</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ram(\alpha)\cap p(B)</annotation></semantics></math> is actually a point of
tangency of <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Br(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Br</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Br(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0\}\times B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0\}\times B</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence
contributes <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> to the intersection number <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=\Br(\alpha)\cdot\{0\}\times B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Br</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=\Br(\alpha)\cdot\{0\}\times B</annotation></semantics></math>. The remaining count, which we want, is
therefore <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e-2[p]\cdot\Ram(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Ram</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e-2[p]\cdot\Ram(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, the count for
<math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e-2[q]\cdot\Ram(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Ram</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e-2[q]\cdot\Ram(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S2.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">The expressions for <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> follow from combining the above contributions.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Returning to the proof of the proposition, consider the following three particular test curves for <math id="S2.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S2.I3.i1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Take <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a family of hyperelliptic curves of genus <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g-1</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by taking a double cover <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\to{\bf P}^{1}\times{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\to{\bf P}^{1}\times{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> branched along a curve of type <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2g,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2g,2)</annotation></semantics></math>. To have sections <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0\}\times{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0\}\times{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\infty\}\times{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\infty\}\times{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, let the branch divisor be tangent to <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0\}\times{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0\}\times{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\infty\}\times{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\infty\}\times{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Take <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> to be a smooth rational curve and <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma{\colon}E\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma{\colon}E\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> a generic cover of degree <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S2.I3.i2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Take <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a family of trigonal curves of genus <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g-1</annotation></semantics></math> obtained by taking a general pencil on <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{F}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{F}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> in the linear system <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|((g+1)/2,3)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|((g+1)/2,3)|</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, or on <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{F}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{F}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in the linear system <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|3\cdot\text{Directrix}+(g/2+2)\cdot\text{Fiber}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>Directrix</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>Fiber</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|3\cdot\text{Directrix}+(g/2+2)\cdot\text{Fiber}|</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is even. Two base-points give <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>. Take <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> to be a rational curve and <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma{\colon}E\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma{\colon}E\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> a general cover of degree <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S2.I3.i3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Take <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{b}{\colon}X_{b}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a family of hyperelliptic curves of genus <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g-2</annotation></semantics></math> as in <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Take <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> to be a smooth genus <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> curve and <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma{\colon}E\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma{\colon}E\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> a generic cover of degree <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d-2</annotation></semantics></math>. This curve exists only for <math id="S2.I3.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S2.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the claim, we get the following non-singular intersection matrix.</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<table id="S2.Ex29.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_markedasmath ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S2.Ex29.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.Ex29.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r"></th>
<th id="S2.Ex29.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S2.Ex29.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S2.Ex29.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S2.Ex29.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.Ex29.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S2.Ex29.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.Ex29.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4d-12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4d-12</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.Ex29.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8g-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8g-6</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.Ex29.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.Ex29.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S2.Ex29.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3g+9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3g+9</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.Ex29.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8d-24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8d-24</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.Ex29.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7g-3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7g-3</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.Ex29.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.Ex29.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="S2.Ex29.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.Ex29.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4d-8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4d-8</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.Ex29.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8g-14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8g-14</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S2.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=3</annotation></semantics></math>, we take a pencil in <math id="S2.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{F}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{F}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{F}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{F}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as in <math id="S2.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, but of trigonal curves of genus <math id="S2.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, without any <math id="S2.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the middle column vanishes, and the second row becomes <math id="S2.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3g+6,0,7g+6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3g+6,0,7g+6)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is linearly independent from the first row.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Degree three</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a curve of genus <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> a map of degree three. The relative canonical map embeds <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> as a divisor in a <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector bundle of rank two and degree <math id="S3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\rm gen}=O\left(\left\lfloor\frac{g+2}{2}\right\rfloor\right)\oplus O\left(\left\lceil\frac{g+2}{2}\right\rceil\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>⌉</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\rm gen}=O\left(\left\lfloor\frac{g+2}{2}\right\rfloor\right)\oplus O\left(\left\lceil\frac{g+2}{2}\right\rceil\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">be the most generic vector bundle on <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of rank <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and degree <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+2</annotation></semantics></math>. Set</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{E^{\rm gen}}:=\{\alpha\in\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\mid E_{\alpha}\cong E^{\rm gen}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{E^{\rm gen}}:=\{\alpha\in\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\mid E_{\alpha}\cong E^{\rm gen}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open subset of <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The complement of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math> is a divisor if and only if <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is even, in which case it is irreducible.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is the degree 3 case of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem13" title="2.13. ‣ 2.1 The associated scroll construction ‣ 2 The Maroni and Casnati–Ekedahl loci ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi{\colon}{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi{\colon}{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the projection. Set</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},\operatorname{Sym}^{3}E^{\rm gen}\otimes{\det E^{\rm gen}}^{\vee})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>E</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>gen</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>∨</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},\operatorname{Sym}^{3}E^{\rm gen}\otimes{\det E^{\rm gen}}^{\vee}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Elements of <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to divisors in the linear series of the line bundle <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}}(3)\otimes\pi^{*}(\det E^{\rm gen})^{\vee}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}}(3)\otimes\pi^{*}(\det E^{\rm gen})^{\vee}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}\subset{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}\subset{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math> be the divisor corresponding to <math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}\subset{\bf P}_{\rm sub}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}\subset{\bf P}_{\rm sub}V</annotation></semantics></math> be the open locus consisting of <math id="S3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="S3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible and at worst nodal. Let <math id="S3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:=\operatorname{Aut}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:=\operatorname{Aut}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> be the group of automorphisms of <math id="S3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> acts on <math id="S3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>. The assignment</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v\mapsto[\pi{\colon}C_{v}\to{\bf P}^{1}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\mapsto[\pi{\colon}C_{v}\to{\bf P}^{1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">gives a map</p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q{\colon}V^{\circ}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}^{\dagger}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q{\colon}V^{\circ}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}^{\dagger}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Denote by <math id="S3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> the preimage of <math id="S3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="S3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}^{\dagger}_{3,g}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}^{\dagger}_{3,g}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The image of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The fibers of <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> consist of single <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-orbits.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For brevity, set <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the
sequence</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0\to O_{{\bf P}E}(-3)\otimes\pi^{*}\det E\to O_{{\bf P}E}\to O_{C_{v}}\to 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\to O_{{\bf P}E}(-3)\otimes\pi^{*}\det E\to O_{{\bf P}E}\to O_{C_{v}}\to 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\pi_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\pi_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\to O_{{\bf P}^{1}}\to\pi_{*}O_{C_{u}}\to E^{\vee}\to 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\to O_{{\bf P}^{1}}\to\pi_{*}O_{C_{u}}\to E^{\vee}\to 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">which says that the Tschirnhausen bundle of <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{u}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{u}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. Conversely, from the Casnati–Ekedahl resolution, it follows that every point of <math id="S3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> is in the image of <math id="S3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v\in U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v\in U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> be in a fiber of <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is an isomorphism <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{u}\to C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{u}\to C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> over the identity of <math id="S3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The sequence (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 Degree three ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) for <math id="S3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> shows that such an isomorphism induces an isomorphism <math id="S3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\to E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\to E</annotation></semantics></math>. The induced automorphism of <math id="S3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> takes <math id="S3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[Picard rank conjecture for degree three]
We have <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Pic}_{{\bf Q}}\mathcal{H}_{3,g}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Pic}_{{\bf Q}}\mathcal{H}_{3,g}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Retain the notation introduced above. For brevity, set <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=U_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=U_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}=U_{E^{\rm gen}}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}=U_{E^{\rm gen}}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}\to U^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}\to U^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> is a quotient by <math id="S3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}\to U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}\to U</annotation></semantics></math> is a quotient by <math id="S3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{PGL}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>PGL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{PGL}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="1.2. ‣ 1.1 Picard groups of quotients ‣ 1 Preliminaries ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="3.2. ‣ 3 Degree three ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U^{\dagger}+\operatorname{rk}\chi(\operatorname{PGL}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>PGL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U^{\dagger}+\operatorname{rk}\chi(\operatorname{PGL}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}V^{\circ}+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}V^{\circ}+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">The final inequality follows because <math id="S3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open subset of a projective space. Let <math id="S3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of divisorial components of <math id="S3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\setminus U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\setminus U</annotation></semantics></math>. We then get the bound</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U+e\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)+e." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U+e\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)+e.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is even, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{PGL}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>PGL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{PGL}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=1\quad\text{by \autoref{thm:maroni3}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mtext>by </mtext><mtext class="ltx_refmacro_autoref"><a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="3.1. ‣ 3 Degree three ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1\quad\text{by \autoref{thm:maroni3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, then</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;l\\
&amp;b\end{pmatrix}\mid a,b\in{\bf C}^{*},l\in H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},O(1))\right\}\big/{\bf C}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>l</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;l\\
&amp;b\end{pmatrix}\mid a,b\in{\bf C}^{*},l\in H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},O(1))\right\}\big/{\bf C}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=0\quad\text{by \autoref{thm:maroni3}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mtext>by </mtext><mtext class="ltx_refmacro_autoref"><a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="3.1. ‣ 3 Degree three ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0\quad\text{by \autoref{thm:maroni3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">In either case, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\leq 2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\leq 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem15" title="2.15. ‣ 2.2 Linear independence of 
          
            T
          
        , 
          
            D
          
        , and 
          
            Δ ‣ 2 The Maroni and Casnati–Ekedahl loci ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.15</span></a>, the classes in <math id="S3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}(\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}(\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g})</annotation></semantics></math> of the two components of <math id="S3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\setminus\mathcal{H}_{3,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\setminus\mathcal{H}_{3,g}</annotation></semantics></math> are linearly independent. Therefore, we get <math id="S3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\mathcal{H}_{3,g}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\mathcal{H}_{3,g}=0</annotation></semantics></math> as desired.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Degree four</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a curve of genus <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> a map of
degree four. The relative canonical map embeds <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> into a
<math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector bundle of rank
three and degree <math id="S4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+3</annotation></semantics></math>. The Casnati-Ekedahl structure theorem provides
the following resolution of <math id="S4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\to\pi^{*}\det E(-4)\to\pi^{*}F(-2)\to O_{{\bf P}E}\to O_{C}\to 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\to\pi^{*}\det E(-4)\to\pi^{*}F(-2)\to O_{{\bf P}E}\to O_{C}\to 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector bundle of rank two and degree <math id="S4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Explicitly, we can describe <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. Write <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=O(a)\oplus O(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=O(a)\oplus O(b)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b=g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b=g+3</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leq b</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> denote
the divisor class associated to <math id="S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{{\bf P}E}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{{\bf P}E}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> the
class of the fiber of the projection <math id="S4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi{\colon}{\bf P}E\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi{\colon}{\bf P}E\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
the curve <math id="S4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is the complete intersection of two divisors</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=Q_{a}\cap Q_{b}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=Q_{a}\cap Q_{b},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[Q_{a}]=2h-af" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[Q_{a}]=2h-af</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[Q_{b}]=2h-bf" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[Q_{b}]=2h-bf</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Even more explicitly, we can describe the equations of <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>
as follows. Write <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=O(m_{1})\oplus O(m_{2})\oplus O(m_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=O(m_{1})\oplus O(m_{2})\oplus O(m_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. Over an open set <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subset{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subset{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y,</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>
denote the relative coordinates on <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E|_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E|_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to the
three summands of <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that <math id="S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}\leq m_{2}\leq m_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}\leq m_{2}\leq m_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Over
<math id="S4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, the divisor <math id="S4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> is the zero locus of a form</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1,1}X^{2}+p_{1,2}XY+p_{1,3}XZ+p_{2,2}Y^{2}+p_{2,3}YZ+p_{3,3}Z^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1,1}X^{2}+p_{1,2}XY+p_{1,3}XZ+p_{2,2}Y^{2}+p_{2,3}YZ+p_{3,3}Z^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction to <math id="S4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of a global section of
<math id="S4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(m_{i}+m_{j}-a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(m_{i}+m_{j}-a)</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, over <math id="S4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, the divisor <math id="S4.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> is the
zero locus of a form</p>
<table id="S4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1,1}X^{2}+q_{1,2}XY+q_{1,3}XZ+q_{2,2}Y^{2}+q_{2,3}YZ+q_{3,3}Z^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1,1}X^{2}+q_{1,2}XY+q_{1,3}XZ+q_{2,2}Y^{2}+q_{2,3}YZ+q_{3,3}Z^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction to <math id="S4.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of a global section of
<math id="S4.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(m_{i}+m_{j}-b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(m_{i}+m_{j}-b)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The irreducibility of <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> puts some restrictions on the possible
<math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, if <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1,1}=q_{1,1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1,1}=q_{1,1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then the section <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X:Y:Z]=[1:0:0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X:Y:Z]=[1:0:0]</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in both <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, making
<math id="S4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=Q_{a}\cap Q_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=Q_{a}\cap Q_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> reducible. An irreducible <math id="S4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> thus forces</p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m_{1}\geq a." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m_{1}\geq a.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> be a vector bundle of rank 3 and degree <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> a
vector bundle of rank 2 and degree <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+3</annotation></semantics></math>. If the locus <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math>
is non-empty, then it is irreducible and unirational.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the dense open subset <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\circ}(E,F)\subset M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\circ}(E,F)\subset M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> that have
<math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}\cong E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}\cong E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}\cong F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}\cong F</annotation></semantics></math>. It suffices to prove the
statement for <math id="S4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\circ}(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\circ}(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the vector space</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V:=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},F^{\vee}\otimes\operatorname{Sym}^{2}E)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},F^{\vee}\otimes\operatorname{Sym}^{2}E).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Elements of <math id="S4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>
correspond to maps <math id="S4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}F(-2)\to O_{{\bf P}E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}F(-2)\to O_{{\bf P}E}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}\subset V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}\subset V</annotation></semantics></math> be the open subset where the ideal generated by the image of
<math id="S4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}F(-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}F(-2)</annotation></semantics></math> defines a smooth curve, simply branched over
<math id="S4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> surjects onto <math id="S4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\circ}(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\circ}(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the dominant map <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}\to M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}\to M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> in the proof of
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="4.1. ‣ 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, it is easy to compute the codimension of
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is</p>
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{codim}M(E,F)=\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(E,E)+\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,\operatorname{Sym}^{2}F)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>codim</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{codim}M(E,F)=\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(E,E)+\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,\operatorname{Sym}^{2}F).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We may think of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(E,E)+\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(E,E)+\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)</annotation></semantics></math> as the ‘expected codimension.’ The next example shows
that the actual codimension is not always the expected codimension.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=O(m)\oplus O(2m)\oplus O(g+3-3m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=O(m)\oplus O(2m)\oplus O(g+3-3m)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil\frac{g+3}{6}\rceil\leq m&lt;\frac{g+3}{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil\frac{g+3}{6}\rceil\leq m&lt;\frac{g+3}{5}</annotation></semantics></math>. To get an irreducible
curve <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, the only possibility for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=O(2m)\oplus O(g+3-2m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=O(2m)\oplus O(g+3-2m)</annotation></semantics></math>, by (<a href="#S4.E3" title="In 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>). The resulting locus
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> is not of expected codimension because <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,\operatorname{Sym}^{2}E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,\operatorname{Sym}^{2}E)</annotation></semantics></math> is nonzero.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Maroni locus <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E)</annotation></semantics></math> may be reducible. Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=12</annotation></semantics></math>, and
consider the bundle <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=O(3)\oplus O(5)\oplus O(7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=O(3)\oplus O(5)\oplus O(7)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the
reader can easily check (using Bertini’s theorem) that <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> are nonempty and of <em id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">equal</em> codimension <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(E,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(E,E)</annotation></semantics></math> for the bundles <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=O(6)\oplus O(9)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=O(6)\oplus O(9)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\prime}=O(5)\oplus O(10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\prime}=O(5)\oplus O(10)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> are two components
of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E)</annotation></semantics></math>. It is easy to see by analyzing the explicit equations
that these are the only components of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>) be the most generic vector bundle on <math id="S4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of rank 3 (resp. 2) and degree <math id="S4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+3</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</p>
<table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\{\alpha\in\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\mid{E}_{\alpha}\cong{E^{\rm gen}}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\{\alpha\in\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\mid{E}_{\alpha}\cong{E^{\rm gen}}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\{\alpha\in\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\mid{F}_{\alpha}\cong{F^{\rm gen}}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\{\alpha\in\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\mid{F}_{\alpha}\cong{F^{\rm gen}}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{{E^{\rm gen}},{F^{\rm gen}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{{E^{\rm gen}},{F^{\rm gen}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=U_{E^{\rm gen}}\cap U_{F^{\rm gen}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=U_{E^{\rm gen}}\cap U_{F^{\rm gen}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">It is easy to see that these are are open subsets of <math id="S4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{d,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{d,g}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our next task is to identify the divisorial components of
their complements.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The subvariety <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:=\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\setminus U_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:=\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\setminus U_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a
divisor if and only if <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is divisible by three, in which case it
is irreducible.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is the degree <math id="S4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> case of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem13" title="2.13. ‣ 2.1 The associated scroll construction ‣ 2 The Maroni and Casnati–Ekedahl loci ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">For the complement of <math id="S4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we could do a careful analysis of the
defining equations of <math id="S4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math>, as we will have to do for the
next case of <math id="S4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=5</annotation></semantics></math>. But we can take a more geometric approach using
the <em id="S4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">resolvent cubic construction</em>. Originally due to Recillas
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rec73</a>]</cite>, the construction can be described as
follows. For simplicity, we give an informal description, restricting
to simply branched covers. See <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cas98</a>]</cite> for a detailed
account. Consider a point <math id="S4.p9.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}]</annotation></semantics></math> of
<math id="S4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math>. The resolution of <math id="S4.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> as an <math id="S4.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{{\bf P}E_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{{\bf P}E_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> module
shows that <math id="S4.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\bf P}E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\bf P}E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is the complete intersection of two
relative quadrics. A fiber of <math id="S4.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}F_{\alpha}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}F_{\alpha}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> naturally
corresponds to the pencil of conics in the corresponding fiber of <math id="S4.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E_{\alpha}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E_{\alpha}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> containing the corresponding fiber of <math id="S4.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each such pencil contains three singular conics, counted with
multiplicity. The total locus of these singular conics forms a
trigonal curve <math id="S4.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(C)\subset{\bf P}F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(C)\subset{\bf P}F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\alpha){\colon}R(C)\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\alpha){\colon}R(C)\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the projection. We call <math id="S4.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> the <em id="S4.p9.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">resolvent
cubic</em> of <math id="S4.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Using that <math id="S4.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is simply branched, it
is easy to check that <math id="S4.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(C)</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth and the branch divisor of
<math id="S4.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with the branch divisor of <math id="S4.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. In
particular, <math id="S4.p9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(C)</annotation></semantics></math> has genus <math id="S4.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+1</annotation></semantics></math>. The association <math id="S4.p9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to R(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to R(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> defines a map</p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R{\colon}\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\to\mathcal{H}_{3,g+1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R{\colon}\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\to\mathcal{H}_{3,g+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p9.2" class="ltx_p">which we call the
<em id="S4.p9.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">resolvent cubic map</em>. The fiber of <math id="S4.p9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> over a point <math id="S4.p9.m25" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[D\to{\bf P}^{1}]\in\mathcal{H}_{3,g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[D\to{\bf P}^{1}]\in\mathcal{H}_{3,g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds bijectively to the set of étale
double covers <math id="S4.p9.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}\to D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}\to D</annotation></semantics></math> (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rec73</a>]</cite> or
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cas98</a>, Theorem 6.5]</cite>). In particular, <math id="S4.p9.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite
morphism.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.6</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> be a vector bundle of rank 2 and degree <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+3</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The
Casnati-Ekedahl locus <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(F)\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(F)\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> is
non-empty if and only if <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor F\rfloor\geq\lceil\frac{g+3}{3}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor F\rfloor\geq\lceil\frac{g+3}{3}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, it is of the expected
codimension <math id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider a point <math id="S4.p10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}]</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> and
its resolvent cubic <math id="S4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\alpha){\colon}R(C)\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\alpha){\colon}R(C)\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(C)\subset{\bf P}F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(C)\subset{\bf P}F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector bundle of rank two
and degree <math id="S4.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g+1)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g+1)+2</annotation></semantics></math>, it must be the Tschirnhausen bundle of
<math id="S4.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(C)</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, we have <math id="S4.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{R(\alpha)}=F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{R(\alpha)}=F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. By
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rec73</a>]</cite>, the map <math id="S4.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, and hence
<math id="S4.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{C}(F)=R^{-1}({M}(F))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{C}(F)=R^{-1}({M}(F)).</annotation></semantics></math> Both of the statements about
<math id="S4.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{C}(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{C}(F)</annotation></semantics></math> now follow from the corresponding statements about <math id="S4.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(F)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.7</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>. The subvariety <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CE:=\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\setminus U_{F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CE:=\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\setminus U_{F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension at least two if <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is even and is an
irreducible divisor if <math id="S4.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is odd.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The image <math id="S4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(U_{F^{\rm gen}})\subset\mathcal{H}_{3,g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(U_{F^{\rm gen}})\subset\mathcal{H}_{3,g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the open locus of
trigonal covers having <math id="S4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math> as their Tschirnhausen bundle. The
complement <math id="S4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z:=\mathcal{H}_{3,g+1}\setminus R(U_{F^{\rm gen}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z:=\mathcal{H}_{3,g+1}\setminus R(U_{F^{\rm gen}})</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension
at least two if <math id="S4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+1</annotation></semantics></math> is odd and it is the Maroni divisor if <math id="S4.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+1</annotation></semantics></math>
is even (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="3.1. ‣ 3 Degree three ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>). The complement <math id="S4.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\setminus U_{F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\setminus U_{F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the preimage <math id="S4.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{-1}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{-1}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the statements
about the codimension follow from the finiteness of <math id="S4.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the question of reducibility, let <math id="S4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=O(k-1)\oplus O(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=O(k-1)\oplus O(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="S4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=(g+3)/2\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=(g+3)/2\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. The claim is that <math id="S4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(F)</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible
when <math id="S4.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g&gt;3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g&gt;3</annotation></semantics></math>, and has two components when <math id="S4.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=3</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(F)=\bigcup_{E}M(E,F)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mi>E</mi></munder><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(F)=\bigcup_{E}M(E,F).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="4.1. ‣ 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, the varieties <math id="S4.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> are
irreducible. Therefore, every component of <math id="S4.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(F)</annotation></semantics></math> must be of
the form <math id="S4.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S4.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g&gt;3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g&gt;3</annotation></semantics></math> and suppose <math id="S4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\neq E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\neq E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>. The inclusion <math id="S4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)\subset M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)\subset M(E)</annotation></semantics></math> and <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem13" title="2.13. ‣ 2.1 The associated scroll construction ‣ 2 The Maroni and Casnati–Ekedahl loci ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a> imply that <math id="S4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> is a divisor if and only if <math id="S4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)=M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)=M(E)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=O(m-1)\oplus O(m)\oplus O(m+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=O(m-1)\oplus O(m)\oplus O(m+1)</annotation></semantics></math>. By choosing two generic quadrics
as in (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E2" title="In 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>), we can
explicitly construct a curve in <math id="S4.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F^{\rm gen})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F^{\rm gen})</annotation></semantics></math>, showing that
<math id="S4.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)\neq M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)\neq M(E)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, it follows that the only
component of <math id="S4.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(F)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E^{\rm gen},F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E^{\rm gen},F)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.8</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The divisor <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\setminus U_{F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\setminus U_{F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not irreducible
for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=3</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, take <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=O(2)\oplus O(4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=O(2)\oplus O(4)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E^{\rm gen},F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E^{\rm gen},F)</annotation></semantics></math> is an irreducible component. Now consider the only
other possibility for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, namely <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=O(1)\oplus O(2)\oplus O(3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=O(1)\oplus O(2)\oplus O(3)</annotation></semantics></math>. By (<a href="#S4.E3" title="In 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>), a cover in <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E)</annotation></semantics></math> must have
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=O(2)\oplus O(4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=O(2)\oplus O(4)</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, for this <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, we can
choose the two quadrics generically and see that <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> is
nonempty. Therefore, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E)=M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E)=M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> is another component
of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\setminus U_{F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,g}\setminus U_{F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Our next goal is to exhibit <math id="S4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a quotient. Let
<math id="S4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi{\colon}{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi{\colon}{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the projection. For brevity, set <math id="S4.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=F^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=F^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set</p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V:=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},{F}^{\vee}\otimes\operatorname{Sym}^{2}E)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Sym</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},{F}^{\vee}\otimes\operatorname{Sym}^{2}E).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p14.2" class="ltx_p">An element <math id="S4.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a map <math id="S4.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}F(-2)\to O_{{\bf P}E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}F(-2)\to O_{{\bf P}E}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>
be the zero locus of the image of this map. Let <math id="S4.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}\subset{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}\subset{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V</annotation></semantics></math> be the open locus consisting of <math id="S4.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V</annotation></semantics></math> for
which <math id="S4.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible and at worst nodal. Let <math id="S4.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{F}:=\operatorname{Aut}({\bf P}F/{\bf P}^{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{F}:=\operatorname{Aut}({\bf P}F/{\bf P}^{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{E}:=\operatorname{Aut}({\bf P}E/{\bf P}^{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{E}:=\operatorname{Aut}({\bf P}E/{\bf P}^{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S4.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{F}\times G_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{F}\times G_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> acts on
<math id="S4.p14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>. The assignment</p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v\mapsto[\pi{\colon}C_{v}\to{\bf P}^{1}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\mapsto[\pi{\colon}C_{v}\to{\bf P}^{1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p14.3" class="ltx_p">defines a map</p>
<table id="S4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q{\colon}V^{\circ}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}^{\dagger}_{4,g}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q{\colon}V^{\circ}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}^{\dagger}_{4,g}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p14.4" class="ltx_p">Denote by <math id="S4.p14.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}_{E,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}_{E,F}</annotation></semantics></math> the preimage of <math id="S4.p14.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{E,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{E,F}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="S4.p14.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}^{\dagger}_{4,g}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}^{\dagger}_{4,g}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.9</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The image of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The fibers of <math id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> consist of single <math id="S4.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-orbits.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is exactly analogous to the proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="3.2. ‣ 3 Degree three ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.10</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[Picard rank conjecture for degree four]
We have <math id="S4.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Pic}_{{\bf Q}}\mathcal{H}_{4,g}=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Pic}_{{\bf Q}}\mathcal{H}_{4,g}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Retain the notation introduced above. For brevity, set <math id="S4.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}=U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}=U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="1.2. ‣ 1.1 Picard groups of quotients ‣ 1 Preliminaries ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem9" title="4.9. ‣ 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U^{\dagger}+\operatorname{rk}\chi(\operatorname{PGL}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>PGL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U^{\dagger}+\operatorname{rk}\chi(\operatorname{PGL}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}V^{\circ}+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}V^{\circ}+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">The final inequality follows because <math id="S4.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open subset of
a projective space. Let <math id="S4.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of divisorial components
of <math id="S4.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\setminus U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{3,g}\setminus U</annotation></semantics></math>. We then get the bound</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U+e\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)+e." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\leq\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U+e\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)+e.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="S4.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=G_{F^{\rm gen}}\times G_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=G_{F^{\rm gen}}\times G_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is an odd multiple of <math id="S4.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{PGL}_{2}\times\operatorname{PGL}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>PGL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>PGL</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{PGL}_{2}\times\operatorname{PGL}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=2\quad\text{corresponding to $M$ in \autoref{thm:4_compUe} and $CE$ in \autoref{thm:4_compUf}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mtext>corresponding to </mtext><mi>M</mi><mtext> in </mtext><mtext class="ltx_refmacro_autoref"><a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="4.5. ‣ 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a></mtext><mtext> and </mtext><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mtext> in </mtext><mtext class="ltx_refmacro_autoref"><a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="4.7. ‣ 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\quad\text{corresponding to $M$ in \autoref{thm:4_compUe} and $CE$ in \autoref{thm:4_compUf}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, but not divisible by <math id="S4.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{PGL}_{2}\times G_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>PGL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{PGL}_{2}\times G_{E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;b&amp;l_{1}\\
c&amp;d&amp;l_{2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;e\end{pmatrix}\mid a,b,c,d,e\in{\bf C},e(ad-bc)\in{\bf C}^{*},l_{i}\in H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},O(1))\right\}\big/{\bf C}^{*}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>e</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;b&amp;l_{1}\\
c&amp;d&amp;l_{2}\\
0&amp;0&amp;e\end{pmatrix}\mid a,b,c,d,e\in{\bf C},e(ad-bc)\in{\bf C}^{*},l_{i}\in H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},O(1))\right\}\big/{\bf C}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=1\quad\text{corresponding to $CE$ in \autoref{thm:4_compUf}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mtext>corresponding to </mtext><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mtext> in </mtext><mtext class="ltx_refmacro_autoref"><a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="4.7. ‣ 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1\quad\text{corresponding to $CE$ in \autoref{thm:4_compUf}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is even and divisible by <math id="S4.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=G_{F}\times\operatorname{PGL}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>PGL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=G_{F}\times\operatorname{PGL}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;l\\
&amp;b\end{pmatrix}\mid a,b\in{\bf C}^{*},l\in H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},O(1))\right\}\big/{\bf C}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>l</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\{\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;l\\
&amp;b\end{pmatrix}\mid a,b\in{\bf C}^{*},l\in H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},O(1))\right\}\big/{\bf C}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=1\quad\text{corresponding to $M$ in \autoref{thm:4_compUe}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mtext>corresponding to </mtext><mi>M</mi><mtext> in </mtext><mtext class="ltx_refmacro_autoref"><a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="4.5. ‣ 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1\quad\text{corresponding to $M$ in \autoref{thm:4_compUe}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is even and not divisible by <math id="S4.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=G_{F}\times G_{E}\text{ where $G_{F}$ and $G_{E}$ are as in the previous two cases,}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> where </mtext><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mtext> and </mtext><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mtext> are as in the previous two cases,</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=G_{F}\times G_{E}\text{ where $G_{F}$ and $G_{E}$ are as in the previous two cases,}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">In all cases, we get</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\leq 3." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\leq 3.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p20.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p20.3.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem15" title="2.15. ‣ 2.2 Linear independence of 
          
            T
          
        , 
          
            D
          
        , and 
          
            Δ ‣ 2 The Maroni and Casnati–Ekedahl loci ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.15</span></a>, the classes in <math id="S4.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> of the three components of <math id="S4.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\setminus\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{4,g}\setminus\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> are linearly independent. Therefore, we get <math id="S4.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\mathcal{H}_{4,g}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\mathcal{H}_{4,g}=0</annotation></semantics></math> as desired.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Degree five</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a curve of genus <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> a map of degree five. The relative canonical map embeds <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> into a <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> bundle <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector bundle of rank four and degree <math id="S5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+4</annotation></semantics></math>. The Casnati-Ekedahl structure theorem provides the following resolution of <math id="S5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\to\pi^{*}\det E(-5)\to\pi^{*}({F}^{\vee}(\det E))(-3)\to\pi^{*}F(-2)\to O_{{\bf P}E}\to O_{C}\to 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\to\pi^{*}\det E(-5)\to\pi^{*}({F}^{\vee}(\det E))(-3)\to\pi^{*}F(-2)\to O_{{\bf P}E}\to O_{C}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector bundle of rank three and degree <math id="S5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g+8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g+8</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Explicitly, we can describe <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. The resolution is determined completely by the middle map</p>
<table id="S5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w{\colon}\pi^{*}({F}^{\vee}(\det E))(-3)\to\pi^{*}F(-2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w{\colon}\pi^{*}({F}^{\vee}(\det E))(-3)\to\pi^{*}F(-2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This
map may be viewed an element of the vector space <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},F\otimes F\otimes E(-\det E))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},F\otimes F\otimes E(-\det E))</annotation></semantics></math>. Due to a theorem of Casnati
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cas96</a>]</cite>, <math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> can be taken to be anti-symmetric, that is, in the
subspace</p>
<table id="S5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V:=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Even more explicitly, we can describe the defining equations of <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. Let</p>
<table id="S5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=O(n_{1})\oplus\dots\oplus O(n_{5}),\text{ where }n_{1}\leq\dots\leq n_{5},\text{ and}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext> where </mtext><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext> and</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O(n_{1})\oplus\dots\oplus O(n_{5}),\text{ where }n_{1}\leq\dots\leq n_{5},\text{ and}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O(m_{1})\oplus\dots\oplus O(m_{4}),\text{ where }m_{1}\leq\dots\leq m_{4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O(m_{1})\oplus\dots\oplus O(m_{4}),\text{ where }m_{1}\leq\dots\leq m_{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We represent an element <math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in V</annotation></semantics></math> by a skew symmetric matrix of forms</p>
<table id="S5.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{w}=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;L_{1,2}&amp;L_{1,3}&amp;L_{1,4}&amp;L_{1,5}\\
-L_{1,2}&amp;0&amp;L_{2,3}&amp;L_{2,4}&amp;L_{2,5}\\
-L_{1,3}&amp;-L_{2,3}&amp;0&amp;L_{3,4}&amp;L_{3,5}\\
-L_{1,4}&amp;-L_{2,4}&amp;-L_{3,4}&amp;0&amp;L_{4,5}\\
-L_{1,5}&amp;-L_{2,5}&amp;-L_{3,5}&amp;-L_{4,5}&amp;0\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{w}=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;L_{1,2}&amp;L_{1,3}&amp;L_{1,4}&amp;L_{1,5}\\
-L_{1,2}&amp;0&amp;L_{2,3}&amp;L_{2,4}&amp;L_{2,5}\\
-L_{1,3}&amp;-L_{2,3}&amp;0&amp;L_{3,4}&amp;L_{3,5}\\
-L_{1,4}&amp;-L_{2,4}&amp;-L_{3,4}&amp;0&amp;L_{4,5}\\
-L_{1,5}&amp;-L_{2,5}&amp;-L_{3,5}&amp;-L_{4,5}&amp;0\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i,j}\in H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{i}+n_{j}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i,j}\in H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{i}+n_{j}))</annotation></semantics></math>. In <math id="S5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math>, the curve <math id="S5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is cut out by the <math id="S5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math> sub-Pfaffians of the matrix <math id="S5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The irreducibility of <math id="S5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> puts some restrictions on the possible
matrices. Indeed, suppose</p>
<table id="S5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1,2}=L_{1,3}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1,2}=L_{1,3}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Then the Pfaffian <math id="S5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> of the submatrix
obtained by eliminating the fifth row and column is</p>
<table id="S5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}=L_{1,2}L_{3,4}-L_{1,3}L_{2,4}+L_{2,3}L_{1,4}=L_{2,3}L_{1,4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}=L_{1,2}L_{3,4}-L_{1,3}L_{2,4}+L_{2,3}L_{1,4}=L_{2,3}L_{1,4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> is reducible, it forces <math id="S5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> to be reducible.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose further that <math id="S5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=O(k)^{r}\oplus O(k+1)^{4-r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=O(k)^{r}\oplus O(k+1)^{4-r}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq r\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq r\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the observation above
implies that the maximum of the degrees of the summands of <math id="S5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\otimes({\det E}^{\vee})\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\otimes({\det E}^{\vee})\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> must be nonnegative, meaning</p>
<table id="S5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}+n_{3}+k-(g+4)\geq-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}+n_{3}+k-(g+4)\geq-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Since the <math id="S5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are increasing,
we get the inequalities</p>
<table id="S5.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}+n_{j}+(k+1)-(g+4)\geq 0\text{ for every $(i,j)$ with $i\neq j$ except $(i,j)=(1,2)$.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> for every </mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext> with </mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mtext> except </mtext><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}+n_{j}+(k+1)-(g+4)\geq 0\text{ for every $(i,j)$ with $i\neq j$ except $(i,j)=(1,2)$.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>) be the most generic vector bundle on <math id="S5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of rank 4 (resp. 5) and degree <math id="S5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+4</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="S5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2g+8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2g+8</annotation></semantics></math>). Define <math id="S5.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> as before. These are the open subsets of <math id="S5.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of covers <math id="S5.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="S5.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, and both <math id="S5.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> are the most generic.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The subvariety <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:=\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}\setminus U_{E^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:=\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}\setminus U_{E^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension
at least two if <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is not divisible by <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>, and has a unique
divisorial component if <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is divisible by <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is the degree <math id="S5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> case of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem13" title="2.13. ‣ 2.1 The associated scroll construction ‣ 2 The Maroni and Casnati–Ekedahl loci ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p8.1" class="ltx_p">For the complement of <math id="S5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we must analyze the defining equations of <math id="S5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The subvariety <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CE:=\mathcal{H}_{5,g}\setminus U_{F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CE:=\mathcal{H}_{5,g}\setminus U_{F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension
at least two if <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+4</annotation></semantics></math> is not a multiple of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> (with the exception
of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=3</annotation></semantics></math> in which case the complement parametrizes hyperelliptic
curves), and contains a unique divisorial component if <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+4</annotation></semantics></math> is a
multiple of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We must characterize the Casnati-Ekedahl loci <math id="S5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(F)</annotation></semantics></math> which are divisorial. We have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(F)=\bigcup_{E}M(E,F)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mi>E</mi></munder><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(F)=\bigcup_{E}M(E,F).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The loci <math id="S5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> are irreducible by
virtually the same argument as in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="4.1. ‣ 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> (In the
proof, just take <math id="S5.p9.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})</annotation></semantics></math>.) Therefore, any component of <math id="S5.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(F)</annotation></semantics></math> must be of the form
<math id="S5.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math>. From the explicit description of degree <math id="S5.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> covers above,
it is straightforward to compute that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{codim}M(E,F)=\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(E,E)+\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>codim</mi><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{codim}M(E,F)=\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(E,E)+\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="S5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\neq E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\neq E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)\subset M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)\subset M(E)</annotation></semantics></math>. By
<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem13" title="2.13. ‣ 2.1 The associated scroll construction ‣ 2 The Maroni and Casnati–Ekedahl loci ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>, <math id="S5.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E)</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension at least two unless
<math id="S5.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=O(k)\oplus O(k+1)^{\oplus d-3}\oplus O(k+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=O(k)\oplus O(k+1)^{\oplus d-3}\oplus O(k+2)</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case,
using the explicit description of degree <math id="S5.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> covers, it is easy to
construct covers <math id="S5.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\alpha}=E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\alpha}=E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}=F^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}=F^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S5.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)\neq M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)\neq M(E)</annotation></semantics></math>, and since <math id="S5.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E)</annotation></semantics></math> is
irreducible, <math id="S5.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)\subset M(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)\subset M(E)</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension at least
one. Therefore, <math id="S5.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,g}</annotation></semantics></math> has codimension at least
two.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, for <math id="S5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> to be divisorial, we must have <math id="S5.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>. In
this case, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\operatorname{codim}M(E,F)=\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes detE^{\vee})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>codim</mi><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{codim}M(E,F)=\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes detE^{\vee}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="S5.p12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S5.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)=1</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=O(n-1)\oplus O(n)\oplus O(n)\oplus O(n)\oplus O(n+1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=O(n-1)\oplus O(n)\oplus O(n)\oplus O(n)\oplus O(n+1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">In this case <math id="S5.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5n=2(g+4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5n=2(g+4)</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence <math id="S5.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> divides <math id="S5.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We are thus reduced to showing that <math id="S5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(E,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(E,F)</annotation></semantics></math> is not a divisor when <math id="S5.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E(-\det E))&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E(-\det E))&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">with the exception of <math id="S5.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=3</annotation></semantics></math>. Write</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=O(k)^{\oplus r}\oplus O(k+1)^{\oplus 4-r}\text{ where }0\leq r\leq 3," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=O(k)^{\oplus r}\oplus O(k+1)^{\oplus 4-r}\text{ where }0\leq r\leq 3,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=O(n_{1})\oplus O(n_{2})\oplus O(n_{3})\oplus O(n_{4})\oplus O(n_{5}),\text{ where }n_{1}\leq\dots\leq n_{5}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=O(n_{1})\oplus O(n_{2})\oplus O(n_{3})\oplus O(n_{4})\oplus O(n_{5}),\text{ where }n_{1}\leq\dots\leq n_{5}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider an anti-symmetric matrix</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{w}=(L_{i,j})\quad 1\leq i,j\leq 5," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{w}=(L_{i,j})\quad 1\leq i,j\leq 5,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">as in
(<a href="#S5.E1" title="In 5 Degree five ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>), representing an element of <math id="S5.p14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H^{0}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})</annotation></semantics></math>. Inequality
(<a href="#S5.E2" title="In 5 Degree five ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>) implies that any contribution to
<math id="S5.p14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})</annotation></semantics></math> must come from the
<math id="S5.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1,2}</annotation></semantics></math> entry. In other words, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E(-\det E))=h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E(-\det E))=h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S5.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}+n_{2}+(k+1)-(g+4)&lt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}+n_{2}+(k+1)-(g+4)&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, we get</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4(-(n_{1}+n_{2}+k-(g+4))-1)-(4-r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4(-(n_{1}+n_{2}+k-(g+4))-1)-(4-r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=4g-4(n_{1}+n_{2}+k)+r+8." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=4g-4(n_{1}+n_{2}+k)+r+8.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p14.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p14.5.1" class="ltx_text">Equation (<a href="#S5.E2" title="In 5 Degree five ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>) tells us that <math id="S5.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}+n_{3}+(k+1)-(g+4)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}+n_{3}+(k+1)-(g+4)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="S5.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{2}&lt;n_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{2}&lt;n_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)\geq(2n_{5}+2n_{4}+2n_{3})-3(n_{1}+n_{2})-6." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)\geq(2n_{5}+2n_{4}+2n_{3})-3(n_{1}+n_{2})-6.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p14.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p14.6.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the two, we get</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))\geq 2n_{5}+2n_{4}+2n_{3}+n_{1}+n_{2}-3(g+4)-2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))\geq 2n_{5}+2n_{4}+2n_{3}+n_{1}+n_{2}-3(g+4)-2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p14.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p14.7.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="S5.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}+\dots+n_{5}=2(g+4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}+\dots+n_{5}=2(g+4)</annotation></semantics></math>, the above inequality becomes</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))\geq(g+4)-(n_{1}+n_{2})-2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))\geq(g+4)-(n_{1}+n_{2})-2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p14.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p14.8.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, by using the assumption <math id="S5.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}+n_{2}+(k+1)-(g+4)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}+n_{2}+(k+1)-(g+4)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{codim}M(E^{\rm gen},F)=\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))&gt;k-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>codim</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{codim}M(E^{\rm gen},F)=\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(E\otimes{\det E}^{\vee}\otimes O(n_{1}+n_{2}))&gt;k-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p14.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p14.9.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S5.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, then we get <math id="S5.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{codim}M(E^{\rm gen},F)&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>codim</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{codim}M(E^{\rm gen},F)&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> as desired. We
consider the cases where <math id="S5.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> on an individual basis. These
cases correspond to <math id="S5.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq g\leq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq g\leq 4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p15" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S5.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case:</span></span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=4</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\rm gen}=O(2)^{\oplus 4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\rm gen}=O(2)^{\oplus 4}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm gen}=O(3)^{\oplus 4}\oplus O(4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm gen}=O(3)^{\oplus 4}\oplus O(4)</annotation></semantics></math>. The relative canonical map embeds <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}\simeq{\bf P}^{3}\times{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E^{\rm gen}\simeq{\bf P}^{3}\times{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The projection to <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> restricts to the canonical map on <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, if <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is non-hyperelliptic, then there is only one quadric in <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> containing the canonical model of <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. This means that the bundle <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> has exactly one <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(4)</annotation></semantics></math> summand, and hence <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\cong F^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\cong F^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>. The locus where <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is hyperelliptic is easily seen to be codimension <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{5,4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{5,4}</annotation></semantics></math>. This exhausts all possibilities in this case.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S5.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case:</span></span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=3</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\rm gen}=O(1)\oplus O(2)^{\oplus 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\rm gen}=O(1)\oplus O(2)^{\oplus 3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\rm gen}=O(2)\oplus O(3)^{\oplus 4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\rm gen}=O(2)\oplus O(3)^{\oplus 4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the special bundle <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=O(2)\oplus O(2)\oplus O(3)^{\oplus 2}\oplus O(4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=O(2)\oplus O(2)\oplus O(3)^{\oplus 2}\oplus O(4)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="S5.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><msup><mi>Ext</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∨</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim\operatorname{Ext}^{1}(F,F)-h^{1}(\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E^{\vee})=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Now consider a general <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}]\in M(E,F)\subset\mathcal{H}_{5,3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}]\in M(E,F)\subset\mathcal{H}_{5,3}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[X:Y:Z:W]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[X:Y:Z:W]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the homogeneous coordinates (locally over <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) on <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to the summands of <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. As usual, denote by <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> the class of <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{{\bf P}E}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{{\bf P}E}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and by <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> the class of the fiber of <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(4)</annotation></semantics></math> is a summand of <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a unique effective divisor <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> of class <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2h-4f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2h-4f</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math> which contains <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. The quadric <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> may be written as the zero locus of a form</p>
<table id="S5.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}Y^{2}+c_{1}YZ+\dots+c_{5}W^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}Y^{2}+c_{1}YZ+\dots+c_{5}W^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are constants. Let <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{\colon}{\bf P}E\dasharrow{\bf P}^{2}\times{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇢</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{\colon}{\bf P}E\dasharrow{\bf P}^{2}\times{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the projection from the section <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[1:0:0:0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1:0:0:0]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g{\colon}{\bf P}E\dasharrow{\bf P}^{2}\times{\bf P}^{1}\to{\bf P}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇢</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g{\colon}{\bf P}E\dasharrow{\bf P}^{2}\times{\bf P}^{1}\to{\bf P}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> the composition with the projection onto the first factor. Then the rational map <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is given by the linear system <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|h-2f|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|h-2f|</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf P}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf P}E</annotation></semantics></math>, which restricts to the canonical series on <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. However, the fact that <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> lies on the relative quadric <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> means that the image <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(C)</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly the conic defined by the equation for <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is hyperelliptic.
Given the above geometric understanding of the <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(4)</annotation></semantics></math> summand of <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>, it is easy to show that if we begin with a hyperelliptic curve <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, and a degree <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> map <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{\colon}C\to{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> must contain a unique <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(4)</annotation></semantics></math> summand. By the inequalities in (<a href="#S5.E2" title="In 5 Degree five ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>), there are no other choices for <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S5.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case:</span></span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=1,2</annotation></semantics></math>. In these cases, we leave it to the reader to see that there are no nontrivial Casnati-Ekedahl or Maroni loci.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S5.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p17.1" class="ltx_p">As before, we now exhibit <math id="S5.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a quotient. For
brevity, set <math id="S5.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=E^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=E^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=F^{\rm gen}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=F^{\rm gen}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set</p>
<table id="S5.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V:=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∧</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V:=H^{0}({\bf P}^{1},\wedge^{2}F\otimes E\otimes\det E).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p17.2" class="ltx_p">An element <math id="S5.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V</annotation></semantics></math> defines an anti-symmetric matrix as in (<a href="#S5.E1" title="In 5 Degree five ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>). Let <math id="S5.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> be the zero locus of the <math id="S5.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math> sub-Pfaffians of this matrix. Let <math id="S5.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}\subset{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}\subset{\bf P}_{{\rm sub}}V</annotation></semantics></math> be the open locus consisting of <math id="S5.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> for which <math id="S5.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible and at worst nodal. Let <math id="S5.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{F}:=\operatorname{Aut}({\bf P}F/{\bf P}^{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{F}:=\operatorname{Aut}({\bf P}F/{\bf P}^{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{E}:=\operatorname{Aut}({\bf P}E/{\bf P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Aut</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{E}:=\operatorname{Aut}({\bf P}E/{\bf P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S5.p17.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G:=G_{F}\times G_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G:=G_{F}\times G_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> acts on <math id="S5.p17.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>. The assignment <math id="S5.p17.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v\mapsto[\pi{\colon}C_{v}\to{\bf P}^{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\mapsto[\pi{\colon}C_{v}\to{\bf P}^{1}]</annotation></semantics></math> defines a map</p>
<table id="S5.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q{\colon}V^{\circ}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}^{\dagger}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q{\colon}V^{\circ}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}^{\dagger}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p17.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.p17.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}_{E,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}_{E,F}</annotation></semantics></math> be the preimage of <math id="S5.p17.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="S5.p17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}^{\dagger}_{5,g}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}^{\dagger}_{5,g}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5.3</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The image of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The fibers of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> consist of single <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-orbits.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is exactly analogous to that of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="3.2. ‣ 3 Degree three ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5.4</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[Picard rank conjecture for degree five]
We have <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\mathcal{H}_{5,g}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\mathcal{H}_{5,g}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is entirely analogous to the proof of
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem10" title="4.10. ‣ 4 Degree four ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>. We indicate only the major steps. Set <math id="S5.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=U_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}=U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>gen</mi></msup></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}=U^{\dagger}_{E^{\rm gen},F^{\rm gen}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="1.2. ‣ 1.1 Picard groups of quotients ‣ 1 Preliminaries ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> to
<math id="S5.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\circ}\to U^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\circ}\to U^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\dagger}\to U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\dagger}\to U</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}U\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S5.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of
divisorial components of <math id="S5.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}\setminus U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}\setminus U</annotation></semantics></math>. We then get</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)+e." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{rk}\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}\leq 1+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)+e.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p19.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.3.1" class="ltx_text">Both <math id="S5.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> depend
on <math id="S5.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> modulo 4 and 5. Using <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="5.1. ‣ 5 Degree five ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> and
<a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="5.2. ‣ 5 Degree five ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, we get the following possibilities.</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<table id="S5.Ex31.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_markedasmath ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.Ex31.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.Ex31.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r"></th>
<th id="S5.Ex31.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\qquad\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)=\operatorname{rk}\chi(G_{E})+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G_{F})\qquad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>rk</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\qquad\operatorname{rk}\chi(G)=\operatorname{rk}\chi(G_{E})+\operatorname{rk}\chi(G_{F})\qquad</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S5.Ex31.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.Ex31.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\mid g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\mid g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.Ex31.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">, <math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\mid g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\mid g+4</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=0+0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=0+0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.Ex31.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text">2 (<math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CE</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.Ex31.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\mid g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\mid g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.Ex31.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text">, <math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\nmid g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>∤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\nmid g+4</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1=0+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1=0+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.Ex31.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text">1 (<math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.Ex31.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\nmid g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>∤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\nmid g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.Ex31.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text">, <math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\mid g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\mid g+4</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1=1+0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1=1+0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.Ex31.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text">1 (<math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CE</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.Ex31.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\nmid g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>∤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\nmid g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.Ex31.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text">, <math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\nmid g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>∤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\nmid g+4</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2=1+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2=1+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.Ex31.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.Ex31.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_text">0.</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p19.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.4.1" class="ltx_text">In all the cases, we have <math id="S5.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{5,g}\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. With
<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem15" title="2.15. ‣ 2.2 Linear independence of 
          
            T
          
        , 
          
            D
          
        , and 
          
            Δ ‣ 2 The Maroni and Casnati–Ekedahl loci ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.15</span></a>, this gives <math id="S5.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\mathcal{H}_{5,g}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pic</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Pic}_{\bf Q}\mathcal{H}_{5,g}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>From Hurwitz spaces to Severi varieties</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The associated scroll construction in <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 The associated scroll construction ‣ 2 The Maroni and Casnati–Ekedahl loci ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§ 2.1</span></a> lets us relate the Picard rank of a Hurwitz space to the Picard rank of a Severi variety. In this section, we work out this relation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the notation <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{g}({\mathbf{F}}_{m},d\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{g}({\mathbf{F}}_{m},d\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{g}({\mathbf{F}}_{m},d\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{g}({\mathbf{F}}_{m},d\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\rm irr}_{g}({\mathbf{F}}_{m},d\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>irr</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\rm irr}_{g}({\mathbf{F}}_{m},d\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#S0.SS1" title="0.1 Notation ‣ 0 Introduction ‣ The Picard rank conjecture for the Hurwitz spaces of degree up to five" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§ 0.1</span></a>. When confusion is unlikely, we abbreviate them by <math id="S6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\rm irr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>irr</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\rm irr}</annotation></semantics></math>. Following Diaz and Harris <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx9" title="" class="ltx_ref">DH88a</a>]</cite>, we enlarge <math id="S6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> by including the irreducible curves of geometric genus <math id="S6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> having a cusp, a tacnode, a triple point, and irreducible nodal curves of geometric genus <math id="S6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g-1)</annotation></semantics></math> (that is, curves having an “additional” node). Denote by <math id="S6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> the normalization of this partial compactification. The local analysis from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx9" title="" class="ltx_ref">DH88a</a>, § 1]</cite> of the Severi variety at points corresponding to cusps, tacnodes, triple points, and an additional node shows that <math id="S6.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth. Since <math id="S6.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> maps to the linear series <math id="S6.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|d\tau|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|d\tau|</annotation></semantics></math>, it carries over it a family of (singular) curves. The normalization of the total space of this family gives a family <math id="S6.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> of curves of arithmetic <math id="S6.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>. A generic fiber of <math id="S6.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\to\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalization the corresponding curve on <math id="S6.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{F}}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{F}}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using the universal family, we can construct tautological divisor classes on <math id="S6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. Consider the diagram</p>
<table id="S6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hbox to65.47pt{\vbox to60.8pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 12.03615pt\lower-49.62325pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} 
{{}}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\hbox{\hbox{{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin} {{}{}{{
{}{}}}{
{}{}}
