<p id="S6.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">The inclusions are open inclusions. <math id="S6.p12.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p12.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> are isomorphic via <math id="S6.p12.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p12.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. The maps marked by <math id="S6.p12.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\star" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋆</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\star</annotation></semantics></math> induce isomorphisms on Picard groups. For the open inclusions, this is because the complements have codimension at least two. For <math id="S6.p12.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\to W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\to W</annotation></semantics></math>, this is because it is a vector bundle.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote the pullbacks of <math id="S6.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> by the same letters. Then, we have</span></p>
